<!-- Airhub vs Instabridge Comparison Content -->
<div class="content-section">

  {% set airhubPrimary = providerA.codes | findCode(providerA.primaryCode) %}
  {% set instabridgePrimary = providerB.codes | findCode(providerB.primaryCode) %}

  <div class="content-callout">
    <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Airhub</strong> usually has the cheaper sticker price per gigabyte before any code is applied, and it bundles in SMS and a local number that Instabridge doesn't. <strong>Instabridge</strong> counters with a much bigger 20% code (against Airhub's 5%) plus a free WiFi hotspot database bundled into the same app. Do the math with both codes applied rather than assuming the cheaper raw price wins: in several countries it doesn't.
    </p>
  </div>

